BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 349.77 Tm (The trap that sinks new operators first is the gap between delivering and getting paid. Giganomic Era warns that direct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 334.55 Tm (clients pay by invoice, sometimes weeks after the work is done, so a fuel cushion has to exist before the first route) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 319.32 Tm (starts [7Mz5ctFZBX0 @ 00:02:11]. Medical Courier Connection puts harder numbers on it: purchasing departments) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.10 Tm (stack approval layers, and a contract nobody read closely can mean 90 days before the first check lands, with routed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 288.87 Tm (work billed at the start of the month and paid in 20-30 days [o1VRiVMJTpY @ 00:04:38]. Ken and Linda also lived) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 273.65 Tm (the credit-card version of this squeeze, funding the business on plastic and watching 'the best like 900 credit rating' fall) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 258.42 Tm (to a 400 credit rating in a single year [o1VRiVMJTpY @ 00:50:26]. Davis's level-one numbers show the same leak on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 243.20 Tm (the app side: a 0.9-mile Roadie delivery paid $8, about $1 a mile typical, and unpaid deadhead 'killed it') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 227.97 Tm ([9oGonGv8OLc @ 00:09:52]. The economics check is blunt. Hold three months of operating expenses, push every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 212.75 Tm (client for ACH, and stack routes so the vehicle earns on every leg, because revenue sitting on an unpaid invoice does) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 197.52 Tm (nothing for a tank that needs filling on Monday morning.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 182.30 Tm (The second cluster of losses comes from paper signed without leverage. Giganomic Era breaks down the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 167.07 Tm (subcontracting math: large-company routes may pay the driver $10 per stop plus a base fee while charging the client) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 151.85 Tm (anywhere from $20 to $50 per stop and double the base [YewfRfz9eUI @ 00:01:26]. The same channel flags one-sided) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 136.62 Tm (termination clauses, where the client can walk immediately while the courier owes 30 days' notice, and tells operators) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 121.40 Tm (to negotiate rate adjustments and fuel surcharges into the deal [YewfRfz9eUI @ 00:06:03]. Medical Courier) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 106.17 Tm (Connection shows what good language is worth: a pay-the-remainder cancellation clause forced a bank client to pay) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 90.95 Tm (out roughly eight months after pulling the work, and charging clients who were free-riding on extras flipped a $35k) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 75.72 Tm (monthly loss into a $35k monthly profit [o1VRiVMJTpY @ 00:27:30]. Alton Arell adds a trap that hits before the first) Tj ET
