BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (revenue.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (Detail: Follow-up cadence comes from Giganomic Era [Giganomic Era - VOBDHU3FYtA @ 00:06:38]; before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (accepting, Sarah Davis checks mileage, schedule, stop count, paid versus deadhead miles, fuel, insurance and operating) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (costs because revenue is not profit [Sarah Davis | The D&G Way - XX29XpCCZO4 @ 00:23:09].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (Advertised rates cluster tightly by vehicle and route type, and the operators read them as ceilings rather than promises.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (Giganomic Era puts Life Carriers contractors at $750 to $1,500 a week on consistent medical routes, with operators) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (running multiple routes well past that, and stresses the money is neither surge nor tip dependent [VOBDHU3FYtA @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (00:01:53]. Eann reads American Expediting's published caps: up to $1,200 a week with a car, $1,500 with a van and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (around $2,000 with a box truck, no cap on commissions, a fuel discount program, and weekly settlement by direct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (deposit or debit card [tidUl8-lql8 @ 00:02:10]. Associated Couriers pays by miles plus stops instead of a flat rate; Eann) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (shows one medical listing at 87 or 89 cents per mile and notes the rate changes by location [tidUl8-lql8 @ 00:05:28].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (On the heavier end, Sarah Davis lists Capstone Logistics in Duncansville, Pennsylvania at $400 to $480 a day for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (extended cargo vans, sprinters and 10 to 16-foot box trucks, on Monday through Friday local routes that start between) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (4:00 and 7:00 a.m. and run 8 to 11 hours, home daily with weekly pay [XX29XpCCZO4 @ 00:08:37]. The pattern) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (holds across every listing: bigger box, bigger number, earlier alarm clock.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (The app layer pays less but fills dead time between contracted work. No Boss Blueprint puts Pills To Me at $14 to $22) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (an hour with instant cash-out, but repeats the common complaint that the background check takes a few days to a week,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (so same-day starts are rare [99Brd_naNps @ 00:01:07]. MedZoomer requires a vehicle under 15 years old plus HIPAA) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (certification, and reportedly pays $21 to $25 an hour on a base rate plus miles driven per delivery [99Brd_naNps @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (00:01:47]. On Roadie, the same channel stresses the advertised $12 is per trip, not per hour, that you request a gig and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (then wait to be chosen, and that prescription runs of a few miles price out around $17 to $25 an hour; their rule is to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (block out a full hour per delivery regardless of the app's time estimate, and medical runs carry no tips that a customer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (can pull [99Brd_naNps @ 00:04:59]. Giganomic Era ranks Dispatch as the best app for rates, consistency and fairness) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (where it operates, reporting $1,000 to $1,500 weeks from a cargo van and $700 to $900 from an SUV, while framing it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (as a commercial platform rather than a guaranteed medical gig [FzfSZhrc8rM @ 00:04:52].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (The scaling mechanics run through vendor and broker channels rather than driver portals. Daeron Myers walks the Lab) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (Express Boston vendor posting: reliable transportation, auto insurance, license, smartphone, an EIN and a company) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm (business bank account, with the vendor expected to provide and oversee seven to 10 drivers across 22 routes averaging) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm ($8,000 per week, more routes than one person can physically run [DMJuDqVtjtU @ 00:04:38]. Myers then explains) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (that Medical Couriers Inc. operates as a broker that does not contract drivers directly and asks applicants not to call) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.35 Tm (dispatch or sales; instead you submit your state, company, number of vehicles and drivers, territory covered and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.12 Tm (insurance level, and the network matches you with carriers that need contract drivers [DMJuDqVtjtU @ 00:07:16].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 160.90 Tm (Sarah Davis shows how a lower-paying listing can be worth more: AME Pharmacy advertises $850 to $1,500 a week,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 145.67 Tm (but because it invites operators to supply delivery personnel, three drivers could push it to $10,000 to $18,000 a month) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 130.45 Tm (in revenue [XX29XpCCZO4 @ 00:07:53]. On price, Boss up with Kae says to always negotiate a fuel surcharge so pay) Tj ET
