BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (form itself is free.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (Insurance is where the unit economics bite hardest. Geoff Cole's for-hire NEMT spec is commercial auto liability with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (a for-hire passenger endorsement at a $1 million CSL minimum, general liability at $1 million per occurrence and $2) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (million aggregate, workers compensation for any W-2 employees, and hired and non-owned auto coverage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm ([dLgmDQavyEU @ 00:06:30]. Nemiton budgets per-vehicle premiums at roughly $5,000 to $10,000 a year in most) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (markets and up to $15,000 in the biggest metros, on top of a typical $1 million commercial auto liability floor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm ([qijT2a0o9VE @ 00:02:09]. Brian Jungeberg's first structural fix is to keep defense costs outside the policy limit: some) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (hired and non-owned carriers fold defense inside the limit, so a $1 million policy that burns $500,000 defending a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (claim leaves only $500,000 of actual protection [0eV-OzFHmX8 @ 00:23:58]. Brian's second fix is errors and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (omissions. Labs routinely demand $1 million in cargo coverage, but cargo pays nothing when a lost biopsy triggers a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (mental anguish or emotional distress suit; professional liability covers that exposure, runs a couple thousand dollars for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (a startup, and doubles as a sales tool when the courier walks the client through why they bought it unasked) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm ([0eV-OzFHmX8 @ 00:27:08].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (The last mechanic is surviving the gap between applying and getting paid. Geoff Cole calls the 60-to-120-day Medicaid) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (enrollment window the dead zone and lists three ways to keep revenue moving inside it: subcontract under an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm (already-enrolled NEMT provider, serve private-pay clients including dialysis patients and skilled nursing facilities, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm (chase broker contracts that do not yet require Medicaid enrollment [dLgmDQavyEU @ 00:05:01]. Nemiton warns that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (even after approval Medicaid pays on a 30-to-90-day cycle, which is why they say to hold 3 to 6 months of operating) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.35 Tm (expenses in reserve before the first trip [qijT2a0o9VE @ 00:05:57]. Jasmine and Monica of MJ Business Academy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.12 Tm (push billing at least weekly, ideally once or twice a week, because states and brokers set a submission window, roughly) Tj ET
