BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 141.78 Tm (The first trap is underestimating what a van costs to keep on the road. NEMT Growth Machine bought a Ford Transit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 126.55 Tm (350 XL with a rear wheelchair lift for $87,900 after taxes and put $6,000 down. The van payment now runs about) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 111.33 Tm ($1,600 a month. The owners call commercial insurance the killer: about $17,315 a year, or roughly $1,440 a month.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 96.10 Tm (Together those push fixed costs right above $3,000 a month before oil changes, tire rotations, or gas [nSB43YYfRs0 @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 80.88 Tm (00:00:20]. Their all-in estimate lands around $43,000 a year, rounded to $45,000 once unexpected maintenance enters.) Tj ET
