BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Getting onto a broker panel is a paperwork grind with a sales layer on top. MJ Business Academy's workflow is simple.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (Go to each broker's website, click the inquiry tab, and fill out the questionnaire. Pre-launch owners can describe) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (themselves as a current provider \("you have two vehicles"\) [KSSO5Igfn2Y @ 00:01:33]. Expect a reply in 5-7 business) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (days listing the required documents. If nothing comes back, resubmit every week, because inquiries get lost) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm ([KSSO5Igfn2Y @ 00:03:35]. Jay at WholeRoute insists you call the broker before you apply and ask three questions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm ([rLXiXIWHxIA @ 00:12:49]:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (1. Are you accepting providers, and what is the trip volume?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (2. What vehicle types do you need?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (3. What are the insurance requirements?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (On the application, list a routing or dispatch software and present your driving experience competitively, though Jay) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (says not to lie. Have a website ready, because half of brokers require one. Plan for a long timeline. Jay budgets about 3) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (months to get in. In one Florida case, a provider with 2 ambulatory vehicles was asked for 4 wheelchair vehicles after) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (waiting 4 months. Only half of applicants get a contract at all [rLXiXIWHxIA @ 00:11:48]. Brokers mostly add) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (providers when enrollment rises. A provider exit creating a vacuum is a "1%" case, and 80-85% of applicants are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (first-time owners competing against established taxi fleets.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (Rates are where, in MJ Business Academy's words, "the battle starts." Never accept the first offer, and keep pushing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (until the broker says "final final offer" [KSSO5Igfn2Y @ 00:05:52]. Broker pay comes in mileage buckets. Trips of 0-3) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (miles start around $12, rates climb to $26-27 on longer buckets, and an ambulatory 5-mile round trip lands around "30) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (something 40." Wheelchair pays more than ambulatory. The low end is brutal. The Southeast Trans sheet Joel Davis) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (reviewed set ambulatory at a $7.23 base with 6 miles included and $1.32 a mile after, and wheelchair at a $17 base with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (6 miles included and $1.48 a mile after [v-IpSBjauKY @ 00:03:12]. A ModivCare holdout in the same video was paid) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (a 14 base and $1.65 a mile ambulatory, and an 18 base and $1.85 a mile wheelchair, with no increase since 2019.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (Georgia under Verida pays more. Ambulatory runs $28-35 base plus $1.35-1.85 a mile, and wheelchair $55-70 base) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (plus $2.75 a mile. Private facility rates there are $65 ambulatory and $95 wheelchair. Verida pays net 21 to net 30 and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (audits heavily in the first 90 days [zXw7440bths @ 00:11:35]. For rate reviews, Nemiton's leverage list is an on-time) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (rate above 95%, a low no-show rate, a review request at 6 months, and a push for multi-year terms [LjAb-IUYxbM @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (00:14:39].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (How you behave inside a broker relationship matters as much as the rate. Davis and his UMTPG team insist that all) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm (correspondence with ModivCare go by email. Brokers push for phone calls because it is part of their training, and calls) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm (leave no paper trail [0Z6CsGngipI @ 00:02:44]. Davis plays deliberately hard to get over email. He calls the broker a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.25 Tm ("pet alligator": you can be friendly with it, but it is not your friend. He advises staying out of network unless the margin) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 244.02 Tm (is good. One out-of-network operator shows the payoff. Brokers offered to raise that operator's rates, Access2Care) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.80 Tm (offered to remove the mileage cap on stretcher rates, and MTM put a credit card on file for a dialysis client) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 213.57 Tm ([xx3dHh731rY @ 00:05:46]. That operator runs about 10 vehicles at seven-figure revenue and roughly 50% margin,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 198.35 Tm (against Davis's target of about 25%. Inside the network, Davis says to cherry-pick and skip the losing trips) Tj ET
